{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"dfb0f393-edb6-4756-9c70-f0ba5a33c76a","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have identified the root causes of the silent failures, fixed the configuration and wrapper script, and documented the analysis in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-FKEuOq/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Root Causes\n\n1. **The job ran 6 times and failed each time**: [launchctl-print.txt](file:///tmp/h-FKEuOq/launchctl-print.txt#L27-L28) shows `runs = 6` and `last exit code = 1`. Every run logged two errors to [nightly-review.err](file:///tmp/h-FKEuOq/Library/Logs/nightly-review.err#L1-L12):\n   - `Not logged in · Please run /login`: [com.vk.nightly-review.plist](file:///tmp/h-FKEuOq/Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist#L23-L29) only set `PATH` in `EnvironmentVariables` and omitted `USER` (`vk`), preventing the headless `claude` CLI from finding its login credentials in the macOS Keychain under `launchd`. Additionally, [nightly-review.zsh](file:///tmp/h-FKEuOq/bin/nightly-review.zsh#L18-L19) passed a multi-line prompt as an argument without piping via `stdin` or closing `stdin` (`\u003c /dev/null`).\n   - `/Users/vk/bin/nightly-review.zsh:19: read-only variable: status`: In `zsh`, `status` is a built-in read-only variable. Assigning `status=$?` caused `zsh` to abort immediately on line 19 before reaching the failure-notification block that invokes [notify.sh](file:///tmp/h-FKEuOq/bin/notify.sh).\n\n### Fixes Applied\n\n- **[com.vk.nightly-review.plist](file:///tmp/h-FKEuOq/Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist#L23-L29)**: Added `\u003ckey\u003eUSER\u003c/key\u003e\u003cstring\u003evk\u003c/string\u003e` under `EnvironmentVariables` so `claude` can access Keychain credentials when launched by `launchd`.\n- **[nightly-review.zsh](file:///tmp/h-FKEuOq/bin/nightly-review.zsh#L18-L36)**:\n  - Replaced `status=$?` with `rc=$?`.\n  - Piped `$PROMPT` via `stdin` (`print -r -- \"$PROMPT\" | claude -p --output-format text \u003e \"$OUT\"`).\n  - Placed the failure notification (`\"$NOTIFY\" ...`) first in the failure path, logged run duration (`SECONDS`), and added a check (`[ ! -s \"$OUT\" ]`) so an empty output file also triggers a failure notification.\n- **[ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-FKEuOq/ANSWER.md)**: Documented the full root-cause breakdown and fixes.\n","duration_seconds":236.07433,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":49007,"output_tokens":12027,"thinking_tokens":8452,"cache_read_tokens":247693,"total_tokens":61034}}}
